# ## Change log for NEMESIS V1.93
# ## March 31st, 2026 
# ##
# ## - Restructured "full_pipeline" to support quaternion pre-fetching before
# ##   LC creation, reducing race conditions in parallel/cluster jobs.
# ##   Three new private helpers added:
# ##       - "_resolve_quat_savepath": canonicalizes quaternion cache directory
# ##         and writes it into default_settings once at pipeline startup.
# ##       - "_resolve_target_sectors": enumerates all sectors to be processed
# ##         prior to any MAST queries.
# ##       - "prefetch_quaternions": pre-downloads quaternion FITS for all target
# ##         sectors; gracefully degrades (RuntimeWarning) on download failure.
# ## - Added "settings" keyword argument to "full_pipeline" to accept a
# ##   pre-built settings dict (e.g. from "default_NEMESIS_pipeline_settings")
# ##   that can be modified before calling the pipeline. **kwargs still take
# ##   precedence over the "settings" dict.
# ## - "get_LC_from_FFI" now returns a 2-tuple (LC_df, sap_diag). "sap_diag"
# ##   is a dict containing SAP diagnostic arrays (bkg_level_per_pix, bkg_trend,
# ##   bkg_residuals, quat_jitter, quat_status, qlp_result, quality_flag)
# ##   for downstream forwarding. Failure paths return an empty dict {}.
# ## - "LC_creation" now returns a 3-tuple (hdu, LC_df, sap_diag) to propagate
# ##   SAP diagnostics through to vetting reports.
# ## - "Transit_Pipeline" updated to accept and forward "sap_diag" kwarg to
# ##   "Vetting_Report_multi_page" and associated page functions.
# ## - Extracted "extract_background_flux" as a standalone function from "SAP".
# ##   Now supports 'median', 'mean', and 'biweight' estimators with iterative
# ##   sigma clipping. Background floor (bkg < 0 → 0) now applied once here
# ##   to prevent inconsistencies between bkgFlux and rawsap_flux downstream.
# ## - Updated "PLD_model" with a two-pass GP-proxy approach for stellar
# ##   variability isolation. Pass 1 runs standard diagonal-ivar WLS PLD.
# ##   Pass 2 uses a biweight-smoothed stellar model to inflate per-cadence
# ##   weights in regions of high astrophysical variability (flares, starspots),
# ##   ensuring PLD fits only systematics. Controlled by new settings key
# ##   "pld_gp_proxy_window" (float, days; set to None to revert to Pass 1 only).
# ## - Unified "plot_it_all_up" replaces "plot_it_all_up_OLD",
# ##   "plot_it_all_up_multi", and "plot_it_all_up_multi_OLD". Single- and
# ##   multi-sector paths are now distinguished by whether median_image,
# ##   pix_mask, and bkg_mask are provided. All SAP diagnostic panels
# ##   (background, quaternion jitter, quality flag heatmap) are forwarded
# ##   via optional kwargs and degrade gracefully when not provided.
# ## - Updated "Vetting_Report_2nd_page_NEW" to forward all SAP diagnostic
# ##   kwargs to "plot_it_all_up".
# ## - Fixed time_chunk unit bug in "Vetting_Report_5th_page_plot_individual_transits"
# ##   (was 3*duration*24 days, now n_dur_window * duration days, matching
# ##   LC time units in BTJD). Also adds model overplot on data-gap panels.
# ## - Added LEO-Vetter wrapper functions as NEMESIS-native implementations
# ##   with consistent formatting: "get_scalar", "format_conditions_block",
# ##   and all 17 FA/FP test functions (weak, invalid_transits, bad_shape,
# ##   non_unique, chases, dmm, single_event, bad_fit, sinusoidal,
# ##   unphysical_duration, asymmetric, chi, data_gapped, odd_even,
# ##   vshaped, large, secondary). Handles numpy/pandas scalar coercion robustly.
# ## - Added "tesssearch_with_radius_growth" for robust lksearch queries with
# ##   adaptive search radius expansion on SearchError or empty results.
# ## - Added "try_apertures" for automated aperture optimization; enabled via
# ##   "do_aperture_optimization" in default_settings. Selects best aperture
# ##   from a grid of thresholds and radii based on a photometric quality score.
# ## - Updated "plot_cutouts" with more robust HDU dispatching to correctly
# ##   distinguish plain Python lists (multi-sector) from astropy HDUList objects.


